author ai
group gui/graph
note The graph canvas is derived, never accumulated. What is on screen is always a base plus an ordered list of expansions: the base is the selected path's steps as a tree, plus the focused symbol as its own root when no step shows it, and each expansion is 'the callers of X' or 'the callees of X' in the order the reader opened them. rebuild runs every frame, reads only the Model, and returns a fresh Built, so closing an expansion also removes whatever was only reachable through it - there is no orphan cleanup because nothing is ever added incrementally. The only state that survives a rebuild is what the reader chose, kept on GraphState: the expansion list, which nodes are cut to a preview, how much context each shows, any node they dragged, and the camera. GraphState's fields are private to the graph module and change only through GraphAction values applied by GraphState::apply, which App::apply reaches through Action::Graph - so every change is an action the rest of the GUI can see, queue or replay. The reader's state is keyed by Node, which holds a SymbolId that a re-index invalidates, so save and restore carry it across one by SymbolKey.

