note The fields split two ways. The reader's part survives frames: expansions opened, auto_open (the off-path root whose callers and callees were opened for it, so closing them afterwards sticks), collapsed (nodes cut to a preview), context (lines widened above and below), manual (dragged positions in fractional cells, which override the layout for as long as the node exists), the drag in progress, pan (pixels) and zoom, and the camera wishes look, hold_look and fit with keep, the node a button asked to hold still. The frame's part is replaced every frame: built (this frame's Built), hits (hit rectangles in window pixels, read by the next frame's input), code_top (the pixel y of each node's first code row) and cell (the frame's cell size in pixels).

